Cleaning Supervisor
Location: Brisbane, Queensland
Employment Type: Full-Time

A growing commercial cleaning company is seeking an experienced Cleaning Supervisor to oversee cleaning operations across multiple commercial sites.

Key Responsibilities:

•	Coordinating and supervising daily cleaning activities across various locations;
•	Monitoring cleaning standards and ensuring work is completed to company requirements;
•	Preparing staff rosters and allocating duties to cleaning personnel;
•	Providing on-site training and guidance to team members;
•	Managing cleaning materials, supplies and equipment;
•	Ensuring workplace health and safety procedures are followed at all times;
•	Liaising with clients regarding operational matters and service delivery;
•	Conducting routine inspections and addressing performance issues where required.

Requirements:

•	Previous supervisory experience within the commercial cleaning industry;
•	Strong organizational and leadership skills;
•	Ability to manage staff and multiple work sites effectively;
•	Good communication and problem-solving abilities.
•	Language skills - English

Please submit your CV and cover letter to; - admin@bmpropertyservices.com.au

Job Objective:                                                                                                                                                                             
The Surveyor is responsible for planning, directing and conducting construction surveying work to determine conformance and set out construction projects;  

Job Tasks and Duties:
Preparing site plans and survey reports; 
Supervising the preparation of plans, maps, charts and drawings to give image representations; 
Conducting all activities in accordance with the integrated management system;
Keeping adequate quality assurance records for each individual task undertaken;
Checking all instruction for relevant quality requirements prior to completion of task;
To operate unsupervised on whatever precision surveys directed or required to do by the Project Surveyor/Management;
High precision conformance surveys as directed or required by the Project Surveyor;
High precision construction set out surveys as direct or required by the Project Surveyor;
Direct/supervise L&L assistant surveyors as required;
Experience required: Bachelor’s Degree in surveying
Full-Time minimum 38 hours per week
Salary: $80,000 to $100,000.00 /year

Phillip Riley are searching for an experienced Corporate Services Manager to
join the executive team. You will report to the Managing Director.

Tasks include:
• Performing high level administration duties and ongoing operational support;
• Comprehensive financial management including planning, budgeting and reporting;
• Strategic initiatives including sensitivity analysis, finance modelling, process reengineering across different operations;
• Ensuring effective ongoing cost control and cash flow management including use of invoice discounting facility;
• Preparing weekly management dashboards and monthly board reports; team management and leadership;
• Liaising with external accountants and auditors when required;
• Performing in public forums to promote new programs and policies
• Ensuring that appropriate systems and internal controls are implemented and maintained;

To be successful in this role, you will be:
• A driven and strategic individual
• Have a keen interest in technology and entrepreneurship
• You will have the ability to combine the growth strategies of several companies while having a hands-on approach to operations and process
improvement.
• Attention to detail
• Great communication and management skills
• A minimum of 1 year experience in a similar role

This role is suited to an experienced yet ambitious individual, with plans to grow into a broader management role.
Salary: $87,500 - $107,500 plus superannuation.
